Phase 19 Task 2 (W1 re-pin): adapt LibRaw's RawSpeed3 C-API shim to the
c835b05a RawSpeed3 API.

`RawImageData::getDataUncropped(x, y)` existed at the old pin de70ef5f
(2021) and has since been removed upstream. Its replacement is the typed
accessor family added in the Array2DRef refactor; the byte-level, uncropped
view is `RawImageData::getByteDataAsUncroppedArray2DRef()`
(RawSpeed3/rawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/RawImage.h:135-136, dispatching to
getU16DataAsUncroppedArray2DRef / getF32DataAsUncroppedArray2DRef at
RawImage.h:330-339). Element (0,0) of that view is the same address that
getDataUncropped(0,0) returned: the first byte of the uncropped image, which
is what `rawspeed3_capi.h`'s `const void *pixeldata` is documented to hold and
what LibRaw reads together with the separately-reported `pitch`.

This is a mechanical API-name substitution; the value handed to LibRaw is
unchanged.

diff --git a/RawSpeed3/rawspeed3_c_api/rawspeed3_capi.cpp b/RawSpeed3/rawspeed3_c_api/rawspeed3_capi.cpp
--- a/RawSpeed3/rawspeed3_c_api/rawspeed3_capi.cpp
+++ b/RawSpeed3/rawspeed3_c_api/rawspeed3_capi.cpp
@@ -178,7 +178,7 @@
         resultp->cpp = r->getCpp();
         resultp->bpp = r->getBpp();
         resultp->pitch = r->pitch;
-        resultp->pixeldata = r->getDataUncropped(0,0);
+        resultp->pixeldata = &(r->getByteDataAsUncroppedArray2DRef()(0, 0));
         const auto errors = r->getErrors();
         resultp->status = errors.empty()? rawspeed3_ok : rawspeed3_ok_warnings;
         return resultp->status;
